Water Quality Investigator - User Guide

What This Tool Does
The Water Quality Investigator is a specialized tool for analyzing water quality in distribution networks. It helps you:
1.	Trace contaminant movement over time through your water system
2.	Identify possible flow paths from any known point or between any two points in the network
3.	Visualize water age, tracer percentage, and chemical concentrations
4.	Analyze specific contamination routes with detailed statistics
5.	View results on interactive maps for spatial analysis
6.	Export analysis data for reporting and further investigation
________________________________________
Data Requirements
Essential Data Needed:
• Network file: EPANET .INP format containing pipe and node data. (If no network is provided, an example network will be loaded. If this application is launched from the main application, the active network will be automatically passed to this module.)
• Geographic coordinates: Latitude and longitude for each node, required for map visualization.
Note: For spatial analysis on maps, your network must include geographic coordinates. Without coordinates, only schematic diagrams will be displayed.

