Key Features Explained
1. Path Exploration
Purpose: Find all possible water flow routes between any two points.
How to use:
1.	Click Explore Paths
2.	Select time period for flow analysis:
o	"Average Flow" for overall analysis
o	Specific time step for moment-in-time analysis
3.	Click START node (source)
4.	Click END node (destination)
5.	Blue lines show all reachable areas from START
6.	Red lines show specific paths to END
Real-world applications:
•	Emergency response planning
•	Source water identification
•	Infrastructure planning
•	Contamination route analysis
2. Interactive Map Visualization
Purpose: View analysis results on geographic maps with detailed pipe-by-pipe information.
Requirements: Network must have geographic coordinates (latitude/longitude).
Features:
•	Multiple base maps: Choose from different map styles
•	Animated paths: Visualize water movement along routes
•	Interactive popups: Click any element for detailed information
•	Network overlay: Show entire system or focus on specific paths
•	Export capabilities: Save maps and data
Access: After using Explore Paths, click "Analyze Paths On Map"
3. Tabular Analysis
Purpose: Get detailed statistics for specific paths or areas.
Available analyses:
•	Links Names: List all pipes in selected paths
•	Links Values: Detailed engineering parameters (flow, pressure, headloss, etc.)
•	Nodes Values: Node-specific statistics (population, demand, elevation, etc.)
Data includes:
•	Water age statistics (max/min/avg)
•	Chemical concentrations
•	Tracer percentages
•	Pressure variations
•	Pipe characteristics (diameter, length, friction)
•	Correlation analysis between parameters
4. Time-based Analysis
Purpose: See how water quality changes over time.
Features:
•	Time slider for navigation through simulation periods
•	Animation of parameter changes
•	Filter by specific time steps
•	Comparison of conditions at different times
5. Filtering and Highlighting
Purpose: Focus on areas meeting specific criteria.
Examples:
•	> 5.0 : Show areas with water age over 5 hours
•	< 0.5 : Show areas with tracer below 0.5%
•	> 2.0 : Show chemical concentrations above 2.0 mg/L
Benefits:
•	Quickly identify problem areas
•	Focus analysis on critical regions
•	Compare different network zones
